1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,016
So, Fatima, Ben, your
survey on remote working,

2
00:00:03,040 --> 00:00:05,532
how many people are
you planning to ask?

3
00:00:05,619 --> 00:00:07,200
About 30?

4
00:00:07,299 --> 00:00:11,360
That's too few for meaningful percentages.
You need 50 at the very least.

5
00:00:12,310 --> 00:00:16,239
For the questions, we were going to
make them all closed. Multiple choice.

6
00:00:16,390 --> 00:00:19,143
That's easier to analyse,
but add a handful of open

7
00:00:19,167 --> 00:00:21,932
questions so people can
explain in their own words.

8
00:00:22,070 --> 00:00:25,471
I'm worried about who we're
asking. Nearly everyone we know

9
00:00:25,472 --> 00:00:29,200
works in an office, so our sample
might end up rather narrow.

10
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:33,920
Then approach a community group. You'll
reach shop workers, nurses, retired people.

11
00:00:34,019 --> 00:00:36,080
Should we give people
something for their time?

12
00:00:36,179 --> 00:00:37,360
What did you have in mind?

13
00:00:37,609 --> 00:00:41,440
A prize draw seems complicated,
so maybe a small voucher?

14
00:00:41,441 --> 00:00:42,265
That's fine.

15
00:00:42,289 --> 00:00:44,720
How long should it take? 20 minutes?

16
00:00:44,769 --> 00:00:48,640
Half that, at the most.
After 10 minutes, people start giving up.

17
00:00:48,789 --> 00:00:51,090
And don't open with the
questions about income.

18
00:00:51,114 --> 00:00:53,772
People find those sensitive.
Put them towards the end.

19
00:00:53,909 --> 00:00:56,320
We were going to try
it out on 5 friends first.

20
00:00:56,419 --> 00:00:59,162
Make it 10, and not just
friends. The main reason

21
00:00:59,186 --> 00:01:01,772
for a pilot is to catch
any confusing wording.

22
00:01:01,809 --> 00:01:03,200
Should we do it on paper?

23
00:01:03,349 --> 00:01:06,560
Use an online survey tool.
The department has a licence.

24
00:01:06,659 --> 00:01:11,040
The biggest mistake I see is questions that
push people towards a particular answer.

25
00:01:11,041 --> 00:01:12,041
Avoid those.

26
00:01:12,239 --> 00:01:15,920
I'll work through the closed
answers using statistical software.

27
00:01:16,560 --> 00:01:19,760
And I'll code the open
answers into thematic categories.

28
00:01:19,859 --> 00:01:22,158
Before any of the
questions, you'll need a short

29
00:01:22,182 --> 00:01:24,252
statement asking for
participants' consent.

30
00:01:24,289 --> 00:01:26,000
How long can we keep the data?

31
00:01:26,149 --> 00:01:30,240
Personal data must be deleted
after a year at the most. 12 months.

32
00:01:30,389 --> 00:01:33,920
And the survey has to be approved by
the Ethics Committee before it goes out.

33
00:01:34,069 --> 00:01:35,520
My approval isn't enough.

34
00:01:35,669 --> 00:01:36,960
How will we report the results?

35
00:01:37,919 --> 00:01:41,360
Not as a written handout.
You'll give a short presentation in class.

36
00:01:41,459 --> 00:01:44,400
And I'd like a draft of your
methodology section by Friday.

37
00:01:44,401 --> 00:01:45,440
And the word limit?

38
00:01:46,259 --> 00:01:49,760
2500, with the final
submission at the end of term.

39
00:01:49,859 --> 00:01:51,680
Thanks. That's really helpful.

40
00:02:13,660 --> 00:02:21,660
Thank you.

